From: avdim <avdimdv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:54:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] chagall-common: audio: Keep AIF2 master for BT SCO mic

bt-sco-hs-mic includes verb-voicecall, which sets "AIF2 Mode" to Slave.
On Master->Slave, the machine driver (adonisuniv_wm5102.c,
set_aif2_mode) stops FLL2. FLL2 is ASYNCCLK, which also clocks AIF3, the
I2S link to the BCM4350. On Wi-Fi models no modem drives AIF2, and only
AIF2 hw_params restarts FLL2. So once a VoIP app opened the BT mic, the
AIF3 clocks stopped and Bluetooth calls were silent in both directions.

Override AIF2 Mode back to Master in bt-sco-hs-mic. In libaudioroute a
direct <ctl> overrides earlier values (last wins); a duplicate from a
sub-<path> would be ignored.

Verified on SM-T800 (Telegram call, Jabra Elite 75t): audio both ways.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I40d7592da08f7345a992fff4cdf750fe7f901d79
---
 configs/audio/mixer_paths_0.xml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/audio/mixer_paths_0.xml b/configs/audio/mixer_paths_0.xml
index c67acfc..96de205 100644
--- a/configs/audio/mixer_paths_0.xml
+++ b/configs/audio/mixer_paths_0.xml
@@ -210,6 +210,10 @@
         <ctl name="ASRC2R Input" value="AIF3RX2" />
         <ctl name="AIF2TX1 Input 1" value="None" />
         <ctl name="AIF2TX2 Input 1" value="None" />
+        <!-- MOD: verb-voicecall sets AIF2 Slave, and the machine driver stops FLL2 (ASYNCCLK)
+             on Master->Slave. No modem drives AIF2 on Wi-Fi models, so AIF3 (BT SCO, codec
+             clock master) loses its clocks -> silent BT calls. Keep Master (ctl: last wins). -->
+        <ctl name="AIF2 Mode" value="Master" />
     </path>
 
     <!--
